== getting_to_orlando ==

Getting to Orlando

Getting here is the unsexy part of the trip and the part most people get wrong. Land at the right airport with the right ground plan and you're in your hotel room two hours after wheels down. Land at the wrong airport with no plan and you're sitting at a rental counter at 11 p.m. with two tired kids and a $400 surprise charge. This page covers flights, rental cars, airport transfers, and driving in. Read whichever section applies to you.

Two airports serve Orlando. Most travelers want Orlando International, MCO. It's the major airport, has direct flights from nearly everywhere in North America and most of Europe, and the rental car center is inside the terminal. Sanford International, SFB, is the secondary airport about 45 minutes north of the parks. It's served almost exclusively by Allegiant Air. If Allegiant flies your route from your home city and the price difference is meaningful, Sanford is fine. If not, fly into MCO.

