== orlando_transfers ==

Airport Transfers (No Rental Car)

Disney's Magical Express, the free bus from MCO to Disney resorts, ended in January 2022. It is not coming back. If you're staying on Disney property without a car, you have four options.

Mears Connect: The closest spiritual replacement for Magical Express. Shared shuttle from MCO to Disney resorts. Cheaper than a private car, slower than a rideshare. Standard service makes multiple stops. Express service is a direct ride but costs more. Reasonable choice for families with kids who don't want to wrangle car seats into an Uber.

Sunshine Flyer: A direct competitor to Mears Connect, similarly priced, similar service model. The two compete on price and reliability. Check both before you book.

Uber and Lyft: Pickup is at the rideshare zone on Level 1 of MCO's terminal. To Disney property is roughly 25 to 35 minutes. To Universal is 20 to 25 minutes. Pricing varies by demand and surge. Best for couples and small groups where the per-person math beats the shuttle. Worst when you have car seat requirements and a lot of luggage.

Private transfer services: Companies like Quicksilver and others run sedan and van transfers, often with car seats included on request. Pricier than rideshare, friendlier for larger groups and families with infants. Several of these are bookable through Viator if you want a single platform for transfer plus park add-ons.

Universal on-site guests: Universal does not offer free airport transfers. Same options as Disney, plus Universal's own SuperStar Shuttle, a paid round-trip transfer between MCO and Universal hotels.

If you're solo or a couple with carry-on luggage, take an Uber or Lyft. If you have kids, car seats, and a week's worth of bags, look hard at Mears Connect or Sunshine Flyer. The math usually favors the shuttle.

